# .rule = forbid-shouted-readme

.what: the repo readme is always `readme.md` (lowercase) — never the shouted `README.md`

read `readme.md`. write `readme.md`. never create, read, or edit a `README.md`.

targets the all-caps `README.md`. mixed-case (`Readme.md`, `ReadMe.md`) is not the shout
this rule names; `readme.md` remains the one canonical form.

.why:
- clones reach for `README.md` out of habit, find no file, wrongly conclude "no readme
  here" — or create a shouted duplicate that drifts from the real one
- one canonical readme per directory prevents `README.md` vs `readme.md` drift
- github renders readme case-insensitively — `readme.md` loses no front-page value
- a specific instance of `rule.forbid.shouts` — shouted filenames shout

.scope:
- applies: every repo-local `README.md` — root, `docs/README.md`, `packages/*/README.md`, any depth
- excludes: `node_modules/**` (third-party), `.git/**` and vendored dirs (not ours)

.canonical form:

| shouted | canonical |
|---------|-----------|
| `README.md` | `readme.md` |
| `docs/README.md` | `docs/readme.md` |

.enforcement: read/write/edit of a repo-local `README.md` = blocker

.note: covers `README.md` only. other shouted docs (`LICENSE`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `TODO.md`)
stay advisorily governed by `rule.forbid.shouts`

.see also:
- rule.forbid.shouts
- rule.prefer.lowercase
